---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { capabilities } from '../../data/about';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Technical Capabilities" description="How my professional practices connect to the technologies, evidence, and learning experiences behind them.">
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p><a href={base + '/about/'}>About</a></p>
    <h1>Technical Capabilities</h1>
    <p class="lead">I find it more useful to explain what I have done, how I approach a problem, and what evidence supports that experience than to assign myself a number on an expertise scale.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capability-approach">
    <div class="body-copy narrative-copy">
      <h2 id="capability-approach">Capabilities live in context.</h2>
      <p>A technology is not a capability by itself. Knowing the name of a tool tells you very little about the questions somebody can answer with it. For that reason, I organize my capabilities around practices, then connect them to the tools, methods, and experiences that give those practices meaning.</p>
      <p>Some of the areas below are grounded in professional work. Others include active personal exploration. I distinguish the two because learning something, teaching something, engineering something, and releasing something publicly are related activities, but they are not interchangeable claims.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capability-domains">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">CONNECTED PRACTICES</p>
        <h2 id="capability-domains">Five areas, many intersections.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Each domain begins with the way I think about the work. Technologies and supporting experience follow, rather than standing in for the work itself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-stories">
      {capabilities.map((domain, i) => (
        <article class="capability-story">
          <div class="capability-story-index" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
          <div>
            <h3>{domain.name}</h3>
            <div class="body-copy narrative-copy">
              <p>{domain.description}</p>
              <p>{domain.perspective}</p>
              <p><strong>Where this comes from:</strong> {domain.example}</p>
              <details class="narrative-detail">
                <summary>Practices, technologies, and supporting evidence</summary>
                <div class="body-copy">
                  <p><strong>Practices:</strong> {domain.practices.join(' · ')}.</p>
                  <p><strong>Technologies and methods:</strong> {domain.methods.join(' · ')}.</p>
                  <p><strong>Evidence:</strong> {domain.evidence}</p>
                  <p>{domain.scope}</p>
                </div>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrative-panel">
      <h2>What these areas have in common</h2>
      <p>I like to understand the structures and assumptions beneath a system, then see what becomes possible when that understanding is put to work. In security, that may mean investigating network evidence. In education, it may mean turning difficult concepts into a sequence someone else can learn. In personal computing, it may mean building an experiment just to find out whether an idea is sound.</p>
      <div class="resource-links">
        <a class="secondary-link" href={base + '/about/experience/'}>Professional experience</a>
        <a class="secondary-link" href={base + '/about/interests/'}>Personal interests</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
